{"kind": "mod", "id": 1349, "name": "Loot Radius", "slug": "loot-radius", "teaser": "Ever get fed up trying to line your crosshair up just right to loot an item? No more! Now loot any loose loot nearby", "owner_name": "DrakiaXYZ", "downloads": 117506, "favourites": 3, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "xyz.drakia.lootradius", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": "Other", "category_id": 17, "updated_at": "2026-07-07T16:58:55.000000Z", "created_at": "2024-04-22T05:56:08.000000Z", "published_at": "2024-04-22T05:56:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~3.11.0", "latest_version": "1.4.1", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<h1>Note: Loot Radius requires a complete rewrite of its grid system due to changes in the latest Tarkov client. The mod will be updated when it’s updated. Do not bother wasting your time attempting to update this mod, it is unlikely I will accept any PRs on this mod</h1>\n<hr />\n<p>Have you ever seen an item you wanted to loot, but just couldn’t quite line your crosshair up on it to pick it up? No more! Now you can open your inventory and loot any loose loot item within a configurable radius that you can see.</p>\n<p>That’s really about it, functionally it’s pretty straight forward, technically it was a major pain to get working. Let me know if you run into any bugs</p>\n<p>Note: Quest Items can not be drag/dropped into your inventory, as they are not standard inventory items. You can Ctrl+Click them to move them straight into your quest inventory</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://streamable.com/e/h2g671\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Preview Video</a></p>\n<h3>Installation</h3>\n<p>1) Open the downloaded zip file in <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.7-zip.org/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">7-zip</a></p>\n<p>2) Select the folder in the zip file in <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.7-zip.org/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">7-zip</a></p>\n<p>3) Drag the selected folder from <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.7-zip.org/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">7-zip</a> into your SPT folder</p>\n<p>Demonstration Video (Yes, it’s Quest Tracker, but the same concept applies to all of my mods, I’m not making mod-specific extraction example videos. No, you don’t need to drop it onto LICENSE-Launcher.txt, just drop it into your SPT folder):</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/mZ1aLrW.gif\" alt=\"mZ1aLrW.gif\" /></p>\n<h3><strong>Configuration</strong></h3>\n<p><strong>Loot Radius (Default: 1.5 meters):</strong></p>\n<p>The distance to look for loot. The center point is the middle of your body, 0.5m off the ground. 1.5m worked well in my testing</p>\n<h3><strong>Compatibility</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>May conflict with True Items and other mods that allow items to stack that don’t normally stack</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you enjoy my work, you can <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://ko-fi.com/drakiaxyz\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">feed my caffeine addiction</a></p>\n", "versions": [{"version": "1.0.0", "spt_version_constraint": "3.8.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 1187, "published_at": "2024-04-22T05:56:08.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1349/loot-radius/1.0.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.0.1", "spt_version_constraint": "3.8.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 15259, "published_at": "2024-04-23T05:39:07.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1349/loot-radius/1.0.1", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.1.0", "spt_version_constraint": "3.9.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 31201, "published_at": "2024-07-06T19:18:48.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1349/loot-radius/1.1.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.2.0", "spt_version_constraint": "3.10.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 24777, "published_at": "2024-11-27T05:16:48.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1349/loot-radius/1.2.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.3.0", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.11.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 3556, "published_at": "2025-03-15T20:01:10.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1349/loot-radius/1.3.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.4.0", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.11.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 1794, "published_at": "2025-03-25T02:43:31.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1349/loot-radius/1.4.0", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}, {"version": "1.4.1", "spt_version_constraint": "~3.11.0", "content_length": null, "downloads": 39732, "published_at": "2025-03-29T02:48:01.000000Z", "forge_link": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/download/1349/loot-radius/1.4.1", "github_url": null, "external_url": null, "local_path": null, "fika_compatibility": "unknown", "dependencies": []}], "repos": ["DrakiaXYZ/SPT-LootRadius"], "source_code_links": [{"url": "https://github.com/DrakiaXYZ/SPT-LootRadius", "label": ""}], "required_by": 0, "no_repo": false, "obtainable": true, "dep_problems": 0}